Two different origins, two different builds, one probe, identical click points.
Flutter-web semantics force-enabled in every run (36 nodes) — with semantics OFF
the defect cannot exist and a pass would be meaningless.

Targeting guards (this bug family has twice been decided by instrument error):
  * targets resolved by EXACT aria-label / EXACT trimmed textContent;
  * among matches the SMALLEST-AREA node wins — the 1440x900 root node matches a
    substring and would otherwise steal the click (the trap that produced a
    confident wrong verdict in both directions);
  * every verdict echoes the chosen rect, the candidate count + their areas, and
    the full document.elementsFromPoint() chain with each layer's role / rect /
    computed pointer-events.

